const faq = [
  {
    q: 'How do I add a provider key without disturbing the one that already works?',
    a: 'Prove it first: <code>POST /api/ai-configs/check-key</code> takes <code>provider</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>base_url</code>, <code>api_key</code> and an optional <code>ai_config_id</code>, and answers whether the endpoint accepted them — storing nothing. Reads mask the key as <code>***</code> plus its last four characters, and an update that sends that masked value back keeps the stored key.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why was my self-hosted model server refused?',
    a: 'Because a tenant-supplied URL is a request the core makes from inside your network. Private and reserved addresses are refused unless <code>ATF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_AI_ENDPOINTS</code> is set, and loopback, link-local and cloud metadata names are refused in every configuration.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which endpoint runs sample text through a prompt?',
    a: '<code>POST /api/prompts/test</code> with <code>prompt_id</code>, <code>ai_config_id</code> and <code>sample_text</code>. It executes the real transform path and answers with the text, the provider and model used, the prompt version and the circuit state — without sending a message.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does a provider outage stop forwarding?',
    a: 'Only if you ask it to. A failed rewrite goes to the task\u2019s fallback policy: <code>SEND_ORIGINAL</code> forwards the original text, while the shipped default <code>DROP</code> fails closed and does not deliver that message.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where is the rewrite switch, exactly?',
    a: 'One gate, two writers. A task rewrites when it has an <code>ai_config_id</code> and its <code>ai_rewrite_active</code> property is true — which it is unless the task metadata carries <code>paid_addons.ai_rewrite</code> and that value is false. The <code>smart_ai_rewrite</code> flag the AI menu writes is reported in the off-path log line but does not switch the pass on by itself.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I check the deployment as a whole?',
